00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,784
听：Finding a Home Near Work.

2
00:00:02,784 --> 00:00:05,568
跟读：Finding a Home Near Work.

3
00:00:05,568 --> 00:00:29,568
听：Daniel accepted a job in a growing city and began looking for a flat. An advertisement described one property as affordable, but the rent was higher than he expected. The landlord also requested a deposit. Daniel calculated his monthly expenditure before arranging a viewing.

4
00:00:29,568 --> 00:00:53,568
跟读：Daniel accepted a job in a growing city and began looking for a flat. An advertisement described one property as affordable, but the rent was higher than he expected. The landlord also requested a deposit. Daniel calculated his monthly expenditure before arranging a viewing.

5
00:00:53,568 --> 00:01:17,184
听：The first flat was close to the office, whereas the second was near a railway station. The nearer he lived to work, the less he would spend on transport. However, the cheaper flat had more space. He realised that affordability depended on the whole budget, not simply the rent.

6
00:01:17,184 --> 00:01:40,800
跟读：The first flat was close to the office, whereas the second was near a railway station. The nearer he lived to work, the less he would spend on transport. However, the cheaper flat had more space. He realised that affordability depended on the whole budget, not simply the rent.

7
00:01:40,800 --> 00:02:05,112
听：A housing adviser explained that a tenant should read the agreement carefully. She asked whether repairs were included and who was responsible for maintenance. Daniel made a list of questions instead of signing immediately. There were fewer vacant flats than he had expected, but he refused to rush.

8
00:02:05,112 --> 00:02:29,424
跟读：A housing adviser explained that a tenant should read the agreement carefully. She asked whether repairs were included and who was responsible for maintenance. Daniel made a list of questions instead of signing immediately. There were fewer vacant flats than he had expected, but he refused to rush.

9
00:02:29,424 --> 00:02:50,592
听：Eventually, he chose to share a flat with a colleague. Their commute was longer, yet their combined bills were manageable. The neighbourhood had a library and a small park. Daniel could now save a little each month without giving up every activity he enjoyed.

